    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Well-differentiated neuroendocrine tumour (NET), oncocytic type",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Oncocytic well-differentiated NET cells are large cells with eccentric eosinophilic granular cytoplasm, coarse chromatin, prominent nucleoli, and relatively plentiful mitoses (Pap).",
    "source": "Michelle D. Reid",
